  <data name="RulesPageTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>How to play Twelve Ranks</value></data>
  <data name="RulesPageSubtitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A brief guide to the rules that differ from ordinary chess.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesStandardChess.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>The goal is unchanged</value></data>
  <data name="RulesStandardChess.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>Checkmate the opposing king. Normal chess rules apply, including check, castling, en passant, stalemate, and standard draw rules.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesBoardAndArmyTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>12 × 12 board</value></data>
  <data name="RulesBoardAndArmyBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each side starts with 12 back-rank pieces and 12 pawns. The wider army adds two Ministers and two Chancellors per side.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesMinisterTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Minister</value></data>
  <data name="RulesMinisterBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Minister moves and captures like a bishop or a knight. It may also exchange places with a friendly king or queen that it can reach, provided the move leaves the king safe.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesChancellorTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Chancellor</value></data>
  <data name="RulesChancellorBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Chancellor moves and captures like a rook or a knight.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesRoyalGuardTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Royal Guard pawns</value></data>
  <data name="RulesRoyalGuardBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The pawns in front of the queen and king are Royal Guards. They may move one square forward, backward, or diagonally, and may advance two clear squares forward from any rank. They do not promote.</value></data>
  <data name="RulesPromotionTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Promotion</value></data>
  <data name="RulesPromotionBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A regular pawn reaching the farthest rank promotes to a queen, rook, bishop, knight, Minister, or Chancellor.</value></data>

