  <data name="ReleaseNoteSummary" xml:space="preserve"><value>Initial development preview of the playable Twelve Ranks foundation.</value></data>
  <data name="ReleaseNoteItem1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Introduced a playable 12 × 12 board with 48 pieces.</value></data>
  <data name="ReleaseNoteItem2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Added Royal Guard pawns, the Minister, and the Chancellor with their custom movement and exchange rules.</value></data>
  <data name="ReleaseNoteItem3" xml:space="preserve"><value>Added local two-player play and a fully offline conventional computer opponent.</value></data>
  <data name="ReleaseNoteItem4" xml:space="preserve"><value>Added legal-move validation and game-state handling for check, checkmate, stalemate, castling, en passant, repetition, the fifty-move rule, and insufficient material.</value></data>
  <data name="ReleaseNoteItem5" xml:space="preserve"><value>Added full undo and redo plus promotion to the queen, rook, bishop, knight, Minister, or Chancellor.</value></data>

